{"tool_name":"mathematica","contents":["neubias"],"fetched_metadata":{"neubias":{"body":[{"format":"basic_html","processed":"<p><strong>Wolfram Mathematica</strong>&nbsp;(usually termed&nbsp;<strong>Mathematica</strong>) is a modern technical computing system spanning most areas of technical computing \u2014 including&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_neural_network\">neural networks</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machine_learning\">machine learning</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_image_processing\">image processing</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geometry\">geometry</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data_science\">data science</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Visualization_(graphics)\">visualizations</a>, and others. The system is used in many technical, scientific, engineering, mathematical, and computing fields.</p>","summary":"","value":"<p><strong>Wolfram Mathematica</strong>&nbsp;(usually termed&nbsp;<strong>Mathematica</strong>) is a modern technical computing system spanning most areas of technical computing \u2014 including&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_neural_network\">neural networks</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machine_learning\">machine learning</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_image_processing\">image processing</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geometry\">geometry</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data_science\">data science</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Visualization_(graphics)\">visualizations</a>, and others. The system is used in many technical, scientific, engineering, mathematical, and computing fields.</p>\r\n"}],"changed":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2020-10-19T15:10:18+00:00"}],"created":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2019-10-16T12:44:37+00:00"}],"default_langcode":[{"value":true}],"attribut